#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275936 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "89462485-2e28-5727-82c7-7afd0cac6d77" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center and Radius of a Circle Given Its Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d49dd980-f027-55ac-9250-4a0d1fb6a46c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(5,-3)$ and the radius is $81$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275938} {:answer/id #uuid "4c8902be-de75-5fb9-886d-39cf4f6d68a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-5,3)$ and the radius is $9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275939} {:answer/id #uuid "57ab104c-0ae2-5bec-8be9-cb72aed64589" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(5,-3)$ and the radius is $9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275940} {:answer/id #uuid "bdfa2c50-eb55-53ef-929f-108c8d57e410" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-5,3)$ and the radius is $81$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275941} {:answer/id #uuid "9c80982b-7787-5617-a49b-78b99aa1a7b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-5,-3)$ and the radius is $9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275942}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4c8902be-de75-5fb9-886d-39cf4f6d68a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-5,3)$ and the radius is $9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275939} :answer-field/id #uuid "aaadfb17-1b72-5e67-8086-0907543d30a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275937}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d5e9656c-2992-5d25-9ed1-710bfe400433" :question/math-academy-id "q-117084" :question/problem "What is the center and the radius of the circle with equation $(x+5)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=81?$" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's compare the general equation to our equation side-by-side as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x+5)^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & =81 \\\\ (x-(-5))^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & ={9}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $a=-5,$ $b=3,$ and $r=9.$ \n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(-5,3)$ and its radius is $9.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275943 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "47863922-b0d5-5a0b-8a01-ffefe3b3c929" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given the Endpoints of a Diameter"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2afa30af-764b-5555-b930-b81c3e13fbc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+{y}^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275945} {:answer/id #uuid "24703135-38c0-5199-acb3-64c112199914" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+{y}^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275946} {:answer/id #uuid "b7e51390-2c92-595d-b4a7-e47b4f0a7f53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275947} {:answer/id #uuid "231d7401-393d-52c1-8e3c-2f29675f718c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275948} {:answer/id #uuid "3ac6739e-cf6f-52ec-8481-099d7d5496ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+(y-2)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275949}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "231d7401-393d-52c1-8e3c-2f29675f718c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275948} :answer-field/id #uuid "46f257a2-b90f-51a3-829a-55339f9fc72e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275944}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "602e9979-5e3e-5ec8-b77b-59541ff9a767" :question/math-academy-id "q-117103" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974570/assets/08653e0cdc9bb404bd7ef193dfc9f1b5c0884002e83dd72cbcbda5779a2363a1.png)\n\nThe line segment $\\overset{―}{XY}$ is a diameter of a circle. Given that $X$ and $Y$ have coordinates $(2,-1)$ and $(2,1)$, respectively, what is the equation of the circle?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the distance formula to compute the distance between the points $X(2,-1)$ and $Y(2,1),$ we find that the length of the diameter is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{(2-2)^{2}+(-1-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the radius of the circle is \n\n$$\nr=\\frac{XY}{2}=\\frac{2}{2}=1.\n$$\n\nSince the center of a circle is the midpoint of the diameter, we can find the center using the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2})=(\\frac{2+2}{2},\\frac{-1+1}{2})=(2,0)\n$$\n\nSo our circle has radius $r=1$ and center $(a,b)=(2,0),$ and therefore it is represented by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+(y-0)^{2} & ={1}^{2} \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275950 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "89462485-2e28-5727-82c7-7afd0cac6d77" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center and Radius of a Circle Given Its Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d3c565c-c49c-55d4-b10b-72ea32d31f15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(3,3)$ and radius is $5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275952} {:answer/id #uuid "077f0fe2-b40d-51af-9812-7476a424b009" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-3,-3)$ and radius is $\\sqrt{5}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275953} {:answer/id #uuid "1b70ece9-a54d-5b0e-9d81-6c970003dedb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(3,3)$ and radius is $\\sqrt{5}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275954} {:answer/id #uuid "6e5cd240-1bdb-5928-a625-8aa1d041f0ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-3,-3)$ and radius is $5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275955} {:answer/id #uuid "71808190-d359-5251-aca3-450cacd2e046" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-3,3)$ and radius is $5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275956}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "077f0fe2-b40d-51af-9812-7476a424b009" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-3,-3)$ and radius is $\\sqrt{5}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275953} :answer-field/id #uuid "c124b45c-0e7b-5924-9007-da3bcb6e0abd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275951}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "905d335a-323b-5d3e-b990-85a375e28da3" :question/math-academy-id "q-70935" :question/problem "What is the center and radius of the circle with equation $(x+3)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=5?$" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's compare the general equation to our equation side-by-side as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x+3)^{2}+(y+3)^{2} & =5 \\\\ (x-(-3))^{2}+(y-(-3))^{2} & =(\\sqrt{5})^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $a=-3,$ $b=-3,$ and $r=\\sqrt{5}.$ \n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(-3,-3)$ and its radius is $\\sqrt{5}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275957 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "47863922-b0d5-5a0b-8a01-ffefe3b3c929" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given the Endpoints of a Diameter"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c6b5918-df87-5e8e-aaae-c22b4e7a1fce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+3)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275959} {:answer/id #uuid "78e9081e-db8a-55e5-8820-0a5e81399707" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-3)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275960} {:answer/id #uuid "c1cac5a7-9ae6-59b4-b6ca-4b0c3714a332" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-3)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275961} {:answer/id #uuid "d90d91fb-3708-5d22-a0ab-2ad22de9e7b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+3)^{2}-(y+3)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275962} {:answer/id #uuid "1a838c54-b3c5-5c40-9683-f92bd7fe8ce7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+3)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275963}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1cac5a7-9ae6-59b4-b6ca-4b0c3714a332" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-3)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275961} :answer-field/id #uuid "82e6df64-4fae-5569-8df0-d3b7494b52b6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275958}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7cc5b5a5-0142-5c39-be39-9d3cacb3c616" :question/math-academy-id "q-70987" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974570/assets/b6a4e9a8f4a1c6dcaaad453b843896f3fc56ae22a37d481dcb4cfe54cc53361d.png)\n\nThe line segment $\\overset{―}{XY}$ is a diameter of a circle. Given that $X$ and $Y$ have coordinates $(7,3)$ and $(-1,3)$, respectively, what is the equation of the circle?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is  \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the distance formula to compute the distance between the points $X(7,3)$ and $Y(-1,3),$ we find that the length of the diameter is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{{(7-(-1))}^{2}+{(3-3)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{8}^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{64} \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the radius of the circle is \n\n$$\nr=\\frac{8}{2}=4.\n$$\n\nSince the center of a circle is the midpoint of the diameter, to find the center we use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2})=(\\frac{7+(-1)}{2},\\frac{3+3}{2})=(3,3)\n$$\n\nSo our circle has radius $r=4$ and center $(a,b)=(3,3),$ and therefore it is represented by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-3)^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & ={4}^{2} \\\\ (x-3)^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275964 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3520d323-c6a4-5bce-bac1-1f4c02bd0068" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given the Center and a Point on the Circle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "025dacac-72b0-5fb3-bd9c-38539d0b355e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275966} {:answer/id #uuid "198f1d79-2b13-51b3-8aa6-bdfc9c72d184" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275967} {:answer/id #uuid "bff52f7b-509c-55f3-a616-d19c98b1c81b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275968} {:answer/id #uuid "cbd780b0-b6fb-5eba-9be5-53b489210677" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275969} {:answer/id #uuid "6ed5618f-9eee-58fa-a504-a8be43554630" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275970}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6ed5618f-9eee-58fa-a504-a8be43554630" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275970} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d7804ea-2943-5975-8ab9-5d3e79f5f2eb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275965}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2d9605a3-33b5-5dbc-a2c1-b1fc1ffe1e35" :question/math-academy-id "q-72619" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974570/assets/2ff035f38f5892f61d1eb037c7e39c59c8ec5104babac45224c4902152a0cfaa.png)\n\nThe circle above is centered at $C(-1,-3)$ and the point $X(1,1)$ lies on the circumference. Find the equation of the circle." :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe length of the radius is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CX & =\\sqrt{{(1-(-1))}^{2}+{(1-(-3))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our circle is generated by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-1))^{2}+(y-(-3))^{2} & =(\\sqrt{20})^{2} \\\\ (x+1)^{2}+(y+3)^{2} & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
